<title>POLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP POOL B RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP POOL B RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KATOWICE, Poland 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the final</p>
<p>day of world ice hockey pool B matches on Monday:</p>
<p> Austria     2     Switzerland    2 (0-0 0-0 2-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Austria - Thomas Searle 44, Herbert Hohenberger 46.</p>
<p>Switzerland - Olivier Keller 56, Andy Naeser 59.</p>
<p> Kazachstan  5     Netherlands    3  (0-1 1-2 4-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Kazachstan - Oleg Kovalenko 25, Andrey Zalipyatskikh 44,</p>
<p>Alexey Trochshinskiy 51, Oleg Kryazhev 57, Pavel Kamentsev 60.</p>
<p>Netherlands - Leonardus van den Thillart 12, 39, David</p>
<p>Livingston 34.</p>
<p> Belarus     6     Britain	  2  (1-0 4-1 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Belarus - Viktor Karatchoun 3, 10, Alexei Lojkin 34, 37,</p>
<p>Andrei Rassolko 30, Alexandre Makritski 60.</p>
<p>Britain - Andre Malo 24, Douglas McEwen 56.</p>
<p> Poland	5     Denmark	  2  (2-0 2-1 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Poland - Zbigniew Podlipni 13, Piotr Zdunek 15, Waldemar</p>
<p>Klisiak 26, Slawomir Wieloch 31, Miroslaw Tomasik 50.</p>
<p>Denmark - Michael Thomsen 40, Struve Larsen 52.</p>
<p>Final standings:</p>
<p>			P    W    D     L     F    A    Pts</p>
<p> 1. Belarus	 7    7    0     0    48   21    14</p>
<p> 2. Kazachstan    7    5    1     1    31   21    11</p>
<p> 3. Switzerland   7    3    2     2    26   21     8</p>
<p> 4. Austria	 7    2    3     2    22   22     7</p>
<p> 5. Poland	  7    2    2     3    19   24     6</p>
<p> 6. Britain	 7    2    1     4    28   22     5</p>
<p> 7. Netherlands   7    2    1     4    21   38     5</p>
<p> 8. Denmark	 7    0    0     7    19   44     0</p>
